{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-11-1","title":"Isaiah 11:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The peaceable kingdom of the Branch out of the root of Jesse. 10 The victorious restoration of Israel, and vocation of the Gentiles.</p>\n<p>And there shall.The prophet having described the destruction of the Assyrian army under that of a mighty forest, here takes occasion to represent the Great Person, who makes the subject of this chapter, as a slender twig, shooting out of the trunk of an old tree; which tender twig, though weak in appearance, should become fruitful and prosper.</p>\n<p>53:2; Zec 6:12; Re 5:5; 22:16 of Jesse. 10; Ru 4:17; 1Sa 17:58; Mt 1:6-16; Lu 2:23-32; Ac 13:22,23 Ro 15:12 a Branch. 4:2; Jer 23:5; 33:15; Zec 3:8; 6:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-2","title":"Isaiah 11:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the Spirit. 42:1; 59:21; 61:1; Nu 11:25,26; Mt 3:16; Joh 1:32,33; 3:34; Ac 10:38 the spirit of wisdom. De 34:9; Joh 14:17; 15:26; 16:13; 1Co 1:30; Eph 1:17,18; Col 1:8,9 Col 2:2,3; 2Ti 1:7; Jas 3:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-3","title":"Isaiah 11:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>shall make him. 33:6; Pr 2:5,9; Lu 2:52 understanding. Heb. scent. or, smell. Job 12:11; 34:3; Php 1:9,10; Heb 5:14 and he shall not. 1Sa 16:7; 2Sa 14:17; 1Ki 3:9,28; Joh 7:24; 8:15,16; 1Co 2:13-15 1Co 4:3-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-4","title":"Isaiah 11:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>But with. 32:1; 2Sa 8:15; 23:2-4; 1Ki 10:8,9; Ps 45:6,7; 72:1-4,12-14; 82:2-4 Jer 23:5,6; 33:15; Mt 11:5; Re 19:11 reprove. or, argue. 1:17; Pr 31:8,9; Jer 5:28 for the meek. 29:19; 61:1; Zep 2:3; Mt 5:5; 2Co 10:1; Ga 5:23; Tit 3:2; Jas 3:13 and he shall. Job 4:9; Ps 2:9; 110:2; Mal 4:6; 2Th 2:8; Re 1:16; 2:16; 19:15 with the breath. 30:33; Ps 18:8; Ac 9:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-5","title":"Isaiah 11:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>righteousness. 59:17; Ps 93:1; 2Co 6:7; Eph 6:14; 1Pe 4:1; Re 1:13 and faithfulness. 25:1; Ho 2:20; Heb 2:17; 1Jo 1:9; Re 3:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-6","title":"Isaiah 11:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>65:25; Eze 34:25; Ho 2:18; Ac 9:13-20; Ro 14:17; 1Co 6:9-11 2Co 5:14-21; Ga 3:26,27; Eph 4:22-32; Col 3:3-8; Tit 3:3-5 Phm 1:9-16; Re 5:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-8","title":"Isaiah 11:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>cockatrice'. or, adder's. 59:5; Ps 140:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-9","title":"Isaiah 11:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>not hurt. 13; 2:4; 35:9; 60:18; Job 5:23; Mic 4:2-4; Mt 5:44,45; Ac 2:41-47 Ac 4:29-35; Ro 12:17-21; Ga 5:22-24; Php 2:14,15; 1Th 5:15 Re 21:27 for the. 30:26; 49:6; 59:19; 60:1-22; Ps 22:27-31; 72:19; 98:2,3; Hab 2:14 Zec 14:9; Ro 11:25,26; Re 20:2-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-10","title":"Isaiah 11:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>in that day. 1; 2:11; Ro 15:12; Re 22:16 which shall. 59:19; Ge 49:10; Joh 3:14,15; 12:32 to it shall. 60:3,5; 66:12,19; Mt 2:1,2; 8:11; 12:21; Lu 2:32; Joh 12:20,21 Ac 11:18; 26:17,18; 28:28; Ro 15:9-12 his rest. 32:17,18; 66:10-12; Ps 91:1,4; 116:7; Jer 6:16; Hag 2:9 Mt 11:28-30; 2Th 1:7-12; Heb 4:1,9-16; 1Pe 1:7-9; 5:10 glorious. Heb. glory. Ps 149:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-11","title":"Isaiah 11:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>set his hand. 60:1-66:24; Le 26:40-42; De 4:27-31; 30:3-6; Ps 68:22; Jer 23:7,8 Jer 30:8-11; 31:36-40; 33:24-26; Eze 11:16-20; 34:23-28; 36:24-28 Eze 37:1-48:35; Ho 1:11; 3:4,5; Joe 3:1-21; Am 9:14,15 Mic 7:14,15; Zec 10:8-12; 12:1-14:21; Ro 11:15,26; 2Co 3:16 from Assyria. 16; 27:12,13; Mic 7:12 Egypt. 19:23; Jer 44:1 Pathros. Eze 30:14 Cush. 45:14; Ge 10:6,7 Elam. Ge 10:22; Jer 25:25; Da 8:2 Shinar. Ge 10:10; 11:2; Zec 5:11 Hamath. 10:9; Jer 49:23; Zec 9:2 the islands. 24:15; 42:4; 66:19; Ge 10:5; Jer 31:10; Eze 27:6; Da 11:18; Zep 2:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-12","title":"Isaiah 11:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>set up. 10; 18:3; 59:19; 62:10; Re 5:9 shall assemble. 27:13; 43:6; 49:11,12; 56:8; De 32:26; Ps 68:22; 147:2; Zep 3:10 Joh 7:35; Jas 1:1 corners. Heb. wings.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-13","title":"Isaiah 11:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>the envy. 7:1-6; Jer 3:18; Eze 37:16-24; Ho 1:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-14","title":"Isaiah 11:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the Philistines. Ob 1:19; Zep 2:5; Zec 9:5-7 toward. 59:19; 66:19,20; Mt 8:11 spoil. 33:1; Jer 49:28; Eze 38:1-39:29 them of the east. Heb. the children of the east. they shalllay, etc. Heb. Edom and Moab shall be the laying on of their hand; the children of Ammon their obedience. 25:10; 34:5,6; 60:14; Nu 24:17; Da 11:41; Joe 3:19; Am 9:12; Ob 1:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-15","title":"Isaiah 11:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>utterly. 50:2; 51:9,10; Zec 10:11 with his mighty. Ex 14:21 he shake. 19:16 shall smite. 19:5-10; Ex 7:19-21; Ps 74:13-15; Eze 29:10; 30:12; Re 16:12 dryshod. Heb. in shoes.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-11-16","title":"Isaiah 11:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>And there shall. 11; 19:23; 27:13; 35:8-10; 40:3,4; 49:12; 57:14 like as it was. 42:15,16; 48:20,21; 51:10; 63:12,13; Ex 14:26-29</p>"}]}